From 5b348ff7eb248c834b4c31583d2205ebddb3d134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Local build <local@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:03:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] EXP effects, QML animations: steady animation clock
 (KWIN_STEADY_ANIMATION_CLOCK)

Mutter 51's timeline pacing (!5157) for KWin: animation time follows the expected presentation
times, but after a dropped or late frame (more than 1.5 refresh intervals) it steps one refresh,
catches up by 1/32 of a refresh per frame and resynchronises when more than 100 ms behind - a
dropped frame is a pause, not a pause and a jump (KWin's own clamp is one 60 Hz frame, so at
240 Hz a dropped frame still doubled the step). Effects' AnimationClock also keeps the fraction
of a millisecond it used to drop at every tick (animations ran 4 % slow at 240 Hz, 14 % at
144 Hz). Off unless KWIN_STEADY_ANIMATION_CLOCK=1.

Plasma/6.8 version (from 82c9fd1b, 2026-10-13): effects get no refresh rate while VRR throttles
repaints for the window that drives it, which skips the steady path for them; QML animations
still get the output's period here. Untested under VRR - the nested guests, where this is on,
have none.
